<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puzrish-Dagan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Drehem</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puzrish-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagan">Dagan</a>, the modern site of Drehem, was an administrative centre near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shulgi">Shulgi</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a> in the late 21st century BCE. It received, recorded and redistributed livestock delivered as taxes and offerings for the temples and the royal household. Tens of thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> tablets from its archives, many looted in the early 20th century, document the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> III economy.</p></div>
